<%# The slate-drop notify-me card: the live countdown to NextSlateDrop and the
    notify-me form, for a visitor with no contest to enter yet. Opened by
    /turf-monster-v2's call to action (pages/_next_contest_cta) with
      $store.modals.open('drop-notify', { title: '...' })
    and registered in modals/_host_extras, the app-wide registration list. The
    engine host owns the dialog: role="dialog", aria-modal, its name from
    props.title, Esc and click-outside close, Tab cycles inside the card.

    ITS ALPINE FACTORIES LIVE ON /turf-monster-v2 (dropCountdown,
    dropNotifyForm), the only page that opens this card. Open it from another
    page and move the factories with it.

    Single root, single quotes only inside x-data: the two rules the host
    imposes on every registered card. %>
<% remaining = NextSlateDrop.remaining %>
<% dropped = NextSlateDrop.dropped? %>
<%# THE HEADER FOLLOWS THE DROP, both ways. The server draws the state it is in
    (the modal opens post-drop whenever no contest is open to enter yet, e.g.
    before the new slate's contests are created), and the x-text keeps it right
    when the countdown crosses the instant with the card open. Each span's
    server text equals its x-text value, so Alpine's first paint changes
    nothing. %>
<%# The header names the slate with an en dash and the drop's date from
    NextSlateDrop ("Weeks 7–9 drops Oct 20"); the form's label below is then
    sr-only, since the header already says what the field is for. %>
<% before_title = "#{NextSlateDrop::LABEL.tr('-', '–')} drops #{NextSlateDrop.drops_at.strftime('%b %-d')}" %>
<% after_title = "#{NextSlateDrop::LABEL} is live" %>
<% when_text = "#{NextSlateDrop.drops_at.strftime('%A, %B %-d')} at #{NextSlateDrop.drops_at.strftime('%-l:%M %p')} Mountain" %>
<% before_sub = "The board goes live #{when_text}. Get one email when it does." %>
<% after_sub = "The board went live #{when_text}." %>
<% js = ->(text) { "'#{j(text)}'" } %>
<%# AUTOFOCUS ON DESKTOP ONLY. The engine host focuses the dialog itself on
    open and returns focus to the opener on close; once the card's open
    animation (320ms, modal-card-mount) has run, a fine-pointer visitor's
    focus moves on to the email field, inside the same trap. On a touch
    device (pointer: coarse) it stays on the dialog: focusing the field would
    raise the keyboard over the countdown. %>
<div data-test="drop-modal" data-dropped="<%= dropped %>"
     x-init="if (!dropped && !(window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches)) setTimeout(function () { var f = $el.querySelector('input[type=email]'); if (f && f.offsetParent !== null) f.focus(); }, 340)"
     x-data="dropCountdown('<%= NextSlateDrop.drops_at.utc.iso8601 %>', <%= remaining[:days] %>, <%= remaining[:hours] %>, <%= remaining[:minutes] %>, <%= dropped %>)">
  <% title_html = tag.span(dropped ? after_title : before_title, "data-test": "drop-modal-title",
                           "x-text": "dropped ? #{js.(after_title)} : #{js.(before_title)}") %>
  <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/card_header", size: :md, icon_emoji: "🏈", title: title_html do %>
    <%= tag.span(dropped ? after_sub : before_sub, "data-test": "drop-modal-subtitle",
                 "x-text": "dropped ? #{js.(after_sub)} : #{js.(before_sub)}") %>
  <% end %>
  <div class="px-5 pb-5 space-y-5">
    <div x-show="!dropped">
      <%= render "pages/drop_countdown_tiles", remaining: remaining %>
    </div>
    <div x-show="!dropped">
      <%= render "pages/drop_notify_form", id_prefix: "drop_modal", test_id: "drop-modal", card: false,
                 stacked: true, visible_label: false %>
    </div>
    <div x-show="dropped" x-cloak class="text-center">
      <p class="text-heading font-semibold mb-3">The <%= NextSlateDrop::LABEL %> slate is live.</p>
      <%= link_to "Play now", contests_path, class: "btn btn-primary w-full" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
